   "subject": "pairs error",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "What’s the underlying reason for an error message like this,\r<br>\r<br>&gt; pairs(fit, pars=c(&quot;theta_1&quot;, &quot;theta_2&quot;, &quot;theta_3&quot;, &quot;theta_4&quot;))\r<br>Error in if (!missing(bandwidth) &amp;&amp; min(bandwidth) &lt;= 0) stop(&quot;&#39;bandwidth&#39; must be strictly positive&quot;) : \r<br>  missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed\r<br>In addition: Warning messages:\r<br>1: In min(x) : no non-missing arguments to min; returning Inf\r<br>2: In max(x) : no non-missing arguments to max; returning -Inf\r<br>3: In min(x) : no non-missing arguments to min; returning Inf\r<br>4: In max(x) : no non-missing arguments to max; returning -Inf\r<br>\r<br>The parameters all exist and, for example, traceplot works fine,\r<br>\r<br>traceplot(fit, pars=c(&quot;theta_1&quot;, &quot;theta_2&quot;, &quot;theta_3&quot;, &quot;theta_4&quot;))"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "34qsW4JDrsUJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2015-06-03T11:55:39Z",
   "subject": "Re: pairs error",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Wednesday, June 3, 2015 at 3:59:59 AM UTC-4, Michael Betancourt wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">What’s the underlying reason for an error message like this,\r\n<br>\r\n<br>&gt; pairs(fit, pars=c(&quot;theta_1&quot;, &quot;theta_2&quot;, &quot;theta_3&quot;, &quot;theta_4&quot;))\r\n<br>Error in if (!missing(bandwidth) &amp;&amp; min(bandwidth) &lt;= 0) stop(&quot;&#39;bandwidth&#39; must be strictly positive&quot;) : \r\n<br></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>It comes from the first line of KernSmooth::bkde2D, which is called by grDevices:::.smoothScatterCalcDensity and autocalculates the bandwidth via<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">        bandwidth </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> diff</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">apply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> quantile</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> probs </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>            </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.95</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> na</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rm </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> names </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))/</span><span style=\"color:#066\">25</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div> </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">  missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed\r\n<br>In addition: Warning messages:\r\n<br>1: In min(x) : no non-missing arguments to min; returning Inf\r\n<br>2: In max(x) : no non-missing arguments to max; returning -Inf\r\n<br>3: In min(x) : no non-missing arguments to min; returning Inf\r\n<br>4: In max(x) : no non-missing arguments to max; returning -Inf\r\n<br></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>Is it possible that two consecutive theta values overflowed to Inf? Does<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">all</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">finite</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">array</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span></div></code></div><br>return TRUE?<br><br>Ben<br><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
