     "<div dir=\"auto\"><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">OK, I&#39;ll look at it later. It only requires the KernSmooth package, but that should be there.<br><br>Ben<br><br>On Thursday, June 4, 2015 at 2:40:38 AM UTC-4, Michael Betancourt wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">It’s the GP model and associated data I sent in the other (private)<div>thread (both model_1 and model_2 have this problem for me).</div><div><br></div><div>There aren’t any required libraries for pairs or anything, are there?<br><div><br><div><div>On Jun 4, 2015, at 12:52 AM, Ben Goodrich &lt;<a href rel=\"nofollow\" data-email-masked>goodri...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Is this model in a repo somewhere?<br><br>On Wednesday, June 3, 2015 at 9:50:03 AM UTC-4, Michael Betancourt wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><br><div><div>On Jun 3, 2015, at 2:55 PM, Ben Goodrich &lt;<a href rel=\"nofollow\" data-email-masked>goodri...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:11px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;float:none;display:inline!important\"><span> </span>it possible that two consecutive theta values overflowed to Inf? Does</span><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:11px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:11px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:11px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code>all<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">is</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span>finite<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">as</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span>array<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>fit<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)))</span></code></div><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:11px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:11px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;float:none;display:inline!important\">return TRUE?</span><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:11px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"></blockquote></div><div><br></div><div>It returns TRUE — the all the samples are well-behaved and I still get</div><div>the error.</div></div></blockquote></div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Stan users mailing list&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send